    pearls: "Vitamin A deficiency is the leading cause of preventable childhood blindness in developing countries. Even mild deficiency (subclinical) increases childhood mortality from measles, diarrhoea, and pneumonia by 20-30%. Bitot spots are highly specific for Vitamin A deficiency but take weeks to months to resolve. Measles infection acutely depletes Vitamin A stores — give Vitamin A to all children with measles per WHO protocol, regardless of whether they have eye signs.",
